cies in openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib (#778)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"jwnasambu","authorEmail":"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a6f911cf3612608cac9649229396e0ebc92ae8ba","date":"2026-08-20T15:59:32-04:00","message":"(test) Add \"golden schemas\" for encounter payloads (#787)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"a72e0f22e6db9b59acc792f5f29fafc6ba25b49f","date":"2026-08-20T21:23:00+03:00","message":"(chore) Bump @openmrs/eslint-config to 2.1.0 (#782)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"77d4275a69960f256411385153379c7aca85630d","date":"2026-08-19T20:55:28-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#788)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"575343c08c8430e8d9de7cd4c137db6a3256c3c4","date":"2026-08-19T14:15:05-04:00","message":"(test) Create \"golden schemas\" for Form Schema operations (#784)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"eb913fd4ca32b7b7c7b4313223709dd9f1b67b5a","date":"2026-08-17T20:55:00-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#786)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"8adafd3e0b530747ff709a9ae25b49d2fa34f2c7","date":"2026-08-14T20:55:32-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#785)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"4db319f4ec64190c6197330675a447dd0121f6df","date":"2026-08-14T17:42:14-04:00","message":"(test) Add scaffolding for better testing (#783)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"7d331d11cab03bd6c5e6e0515bf9a4b2416dfdac","date":"2026-08-13T20:55:37-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#781)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"380ea216b27ee0925d097e8e1aef5f9a32c4dee6","date":"2026-08-12T20:55:19-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#780)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"fed294cb652b1873f64a738b8b5b7b9424b93189","date":"2026-08-12T11:06:00+03:00","message":"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#779)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9\n\nLint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing .eslintrc and .eslintignore. eslint\nmoves from 8.57 to ^9.39.0 and the --ext flag goes away, since flat config\nmakes it redundant. The .d.ts ignore is kept, and dist and coverage are\nnamed explicitly.\n\nComparing the effective rule sets before and after, six rules would have\nbeen lost, so the overlay enforces them again: ban-ts-comment,\ntriple-slash-reference, no-extra-boolean-cast, no-prototype-builtins,\nno-unsafe-optional-chaining and no-useless-escape. This repo disabled\nban-types deliberately, so the rules typescript-eslint v8 split it into stay\noff, unlike other repos in this migration.\n\nThe old config also loaded type information through parserOptions.project\nwhile enabling no type-aware rules, so that cost goes away with it. Four dev\ndependencies go with the plugins the shared config provides, including\neslint-plugin-jsx-a11y, which was declared but never referenced.\n\nThe shared config lints tests with testing-library and jest-dom for the\nfirst time here, which reported 97 problems across the test suite. Sixteen\nwere autofixes. no-unused-expressions found a real one:\nexpect(...).toBeInTheDocument was missing its call, so that assertion never\nran. It passes now that it does. The rule keeps reporting, with\nallowShortCircuit set, because `x && f()` as a statement is an idiom here.\n\nThe remaining 76 are no-unnecessary-act, render-result-naming-convention\nand no-manual-cleanup. Those need the tests reworked rather than\nreformatted, so they are off for test files until that happens, and the rest\nof testing-library applies.\n\n__mocks__/index.ts loads JSON fixtures with require(). The shared config\nexempts __mocks__/**/*.js from no-require-imports but these mocks are\nTypeScript, so the exemption is repeated here for the directory.\n\n* Keep ESLint config out of next updates\n\nReplace the @openmrs wildcard with the packages this repository actually tracks on the next tag. This prevents the stable-only ESLint config from breaking the scheduled dependency update workflow.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b7a344d184b2002dc0babbcb5bba1d37d29ea51b","date":"2026-08-07T20:55:06-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#777)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"645075caed1459277a419db89fe419e4c80274e8","date":"2026-08-05T21:03:59-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#775)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"d13f4fe33fb0697e2e57208bafa0b34a256ef547","date":"2026-08-04T21:03:50-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#774)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"93d5d8f72290a51a4d03e97376f6d54a057d796b","date":"2026-08-01T21:09:03-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#773)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"7fbe50b5466e6913d6100594214d10ea2e71d77b","date":"2026-07-31T21:07:08-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#772)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"86da0a4e77715ffcc4af84f7d7cb9f9b826dc5de",