{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxP61oLD9UDMggqcdgotLW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"3a4f5da7161780ab37e381c96a69656bcb87ee8a","date":"2026-05-29T00:58:07-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#748)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"b3677e993d890413c28224f0a993fdf29742246c","date":"2026-05-27T01:01:24-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#747)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"d83f538b619ce2c11012b88cfc3f461f2e7c8a48","date":"2026-05-23T00:30:24-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#746)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"c3db611b3b20f63ad06900d74b5cabf8ad67f1e5","date":"2026-05-22T00:49:28-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#745)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"943417485df73db15899950dc546856f0a9c430b","date":"2026-05-21T00:58:29-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#744)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"78c90e22a7f1b98a727b7a87fc8d72a715ed7295","date":"2026-05-14T00:33:15-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#743)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"bda295eac9755a4df1c22c9c024ea987ccf4d339","date":"2026-05-14T01:18:07+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5660: Encounter provider field should auto-fill with current session provider on new forms (#740)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Donald Kibet","authorEmail":"chelashawdonald@yahoo.com"},{"hash":"2204ac05b44795dec06b132c0d15ca1b010bcd95","date":"2026-05-13T16:35:49+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#742)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, aligning form-engine-lib\nwith the patterns adopted across the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom, and\n  @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and cross-env.\n  Bump @testing-library/dom (9.x to 10.x), @testing-library/jest-dom\n  (6.4 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react (14.x to 16.x) so the\n  /vitest subpath is available. Keep jest-when on jest-when@^3.x: its\n  fluent API works against vitest's vi.fn() unchanged because vitest\n  mocks are jest-API-compatible.\n- Add vitest.config.ts: jsdom environment, .scss/.css aliased to\n  identity-obj-proxy via the anchored ^.*\\.s?css$ regex,\n  @openmrs/esm-framework aliased to its mock, react-i18next and\n  react-markdown aliased to their local __mocks__ files,\n  __mocks__/* and src/* aliased so the bare imports the jest\n  config used to resolve via moduleDirectories continue to work,\n  and fakeTimers.toFake limited so it does not break React's\n  scheduler.\n- Replace src/setup-tests.ts's '@testing-library/jest-dom' import\n  with '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest', drop the 'jest-when'\n  side-effect import (no longer needed), swap jest.fn for vi.fn in\n  the i18next mock, and convert the require('resize-observer-polyfill')\n  call to a proper ESM import.\n- Rewrite __mocks__/react-i18next.js's I18nextProvider entry to a\n  plain function component, since the previous jest.fn() call only\n  worked under jest's globals.\n- Convert the 41 test files to the vitest API: explicit imports for\n  describe/expect/it/test/vi (plus beforeEach/afterEach/type Mock\n  where used), jest.* swapped for vi.*. The many vi.mock(path, ...\n  jest.requireActual(path), override) factories rewritten as the\n  async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await vi.importActual(path))\n  as object), override })) form. The vi.mock(name, () => vi.fn())\n  factory wrapped in { default: vi.fn() }. The jest.requireMock call\n  in usePostSubmissionActions.test.tsx replaced with vi.mocked over\n  a direct import. The pre-existing xdescribe rewritten as\n  describe.skip. fail() calls swapped for expect.fail().\n  vi.spyOn(...).mockImplementation() calls passed an explicit\n  () => {} since vitest's mockImplementation requires an argument.\n- Skip 8 tests that were exercising Carbon UiSelectExtended or\n  fake-timer + ART-month-calc flows; they appear to depend on\n  jest-fake-timers semantics or Carbon DOM details that do not\n  reproduce in jsdom under vitest. Each carries a TODO comment for\n  follow-up. The remaining 343 tests pass.\n- Delete jest.config.js.\n\n343 tests pass (20 skipped, 12 of which were skipped pre-existing).\nLint and typescript checks are green.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath for vitest config aliases\n\nnew URL('./path', import.meta.url).pathname returns /C:/Users/... on\nWindows, which is not a valid filesystem path for Node's fs or\npath.resolve. The seven alias replacements in vitest.config.ts all\nrelied on .pathname, so the test suite would have silently broken for\nWindows contributors.\n\nAdd a small helper that wraps fileURLToPath so each call site stays\nreadable, and route every URL-based path through it.\n\nAlso update tsconfig.json to include vitest.config.ts and drop the\nstale references to setupTests.ts (the actual file lives under src/)\nand jest.config.js (deleted in this PR). Without vitest.config.ts in\nthe include list, typed eslint refuses to lint it.\n\n* (chore) Document why specific tests are skipped during vitest migration\n\nFive tests / blocks were skipped during the jest-to-vitest migration\nwithout an inline marker explaining the symptom or who is expected to\nunskip them. Add a TODO comment above each:\n\n- ui-select-extended 'Enter/New mode' and 'Edit mode': the Carbon\n  UiSelectExtended combobox no longer exposes its options to the\n  accessible-name queries the tests rely on under jsdom +\n  @testing-library/react 16.\n- form-engine 'should evaluate months on ART': the test wired up\n  jest-fake-timers' doNotFake option, which vitest's fakeTimers API\n  does not provide a direct equivalent for.\n- form-engine 'should save diagnosis field on form submission' and\n  'should edit diagnosis field on form submission': the Carbon\n  combobox in the diagnosis-search workspace has the same option\n  discoverability issue as ui-select-extended.\n\nNo behaviour change; comments only.\n\n* (chore) Move setup-tests.ts out of src/ into tools/\n\nPer review feedback: this file is test infrastructure, not library\nsource, so it doesn't belong under src/. Matches the convention used in\nother recent PRs in this repo.\n\n- src/setup-tests.ts → tools/setup-tests.ts\n- vitest.config.ts: setupFiles path updated\n- tsconfig.json: add tools/setup-tests.ts to include (the previous\n  src/**/* glob picked it up; now it's outside that glob)\n- package.json: drop the now-redundant \"!src/setup-tests.ts\" files\n  exclusion (the file is no longer in src/)\n\nThe build script's \"--ignore '**/setup-tests.*'\" pattern and\ntsconfig.build.json's exclude pattern still match by basename, so no\nchange there.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"335ccfb562bee8ea8fa8ddd919d78ba32139c644","date":"2026-05-12T00:27:41-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#741)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"2bc77fd37df11bf1830be463bd42e49870f85030","date":"2026-05-09T00:07:34-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#739)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"4780add7888b64f467f292dbc88985227a9ab420","date":"2026-05-07T14:08:23-04:00","message":"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#738)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"openmrs-bot","authorEmail":"infrastructure@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"5a53d9996f8aadb66200869d