{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KhGLE3CFwP8b8VGzB9dKPB","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","number":826,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write","state":"merged","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-10-01T10:15:15.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-10-05T11:52:42.000Z","closedAt":"2026-10-05T11:52:42.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/pull/826","mergeCommit":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","syncedAt":"2026-10-24T04:03:09.520Z","tickets":[{"key":"O3-6027","source":"ticket-pattern"}],"commits":[{"sha":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files":[{"path":"src/adapters/encounter-diagnosis-adapter.test.ts","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/adapters/encounter-diagnosis-adapter.ts","additions":2,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/adapters/orders-adapter.ts","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"path":"src/processors/encounter/encounter-payloads.golden.test.ts","additions":97,"deletions":22}],"body":"## Requirements\n\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe orders and diagnosis adapters now clear the field's submission at the start of `transformFieldValue`, the same way `ObsAdapter` already does.\n\nBefore this, a value from an earlier write stayed on the field after it was cleared, because `gracefullySetSubmission` only sets values and never clears them. On a new encounter, if you selected an order or diagnosis and then cleared the field, it still went out with the encounter. On an edited encounter, if you swapped a saved order or diagnosis for another value and then cleared the field, the swapped value still went out. For orders that meant a `NEW` order alongside the void. For diagnoses it meant the saved diagnosis got edited to the swapped concept instead of being voided. Now nothing is submitted for a new encounter, and only the void goes out for an edited one.\n\n`editOrder` no longer calls `clearSubmission` itself when the value matches the saved order, since the submission is already empty by then.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n## Related Issue\n\n## Other\n\nI found this while working on #822. It's the reason a swap followed by a clear still keeps the saved order or diagnosis when the field is hidden there. With both merged, that case voids it like any other cleared value.\n","freshness":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","lastSyncedAt":"2026-10-24T04:03:09.520Z","stale":false}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ca5d02f-4799-48ab-8f7a-1e5280f8de08","uuid":"2b3f6821-35d2-451a-b8f3-ccabfcaba1d4","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:04:32.391Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","number":826,"kind":"pr","title":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write","state":"merged","author":"denniskigen","createdAt":"2026-10-01T10:15:15.000Z","mergedAt":"2026-10-05T11:52:42.000Z","closedAt":"2026-10-05T11:52:42.000Z","url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib/pull/826","mergeCommit":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","syncedAt":"2026-10-24T04:03:09.520Z","tickets":[{"key":"O3-6027","source":"ticket-pattern"}],"commits":[{"sha":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","source":"merge-commit-sha","verified":true}],"files